===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A heavy or helpless collapse; a slouching or drooping [[posture]]; a period of poor activity or performance, especially an [[extended]] period.
# A measure of the fluidity of freshly mixed concrete, based on how much the concrete formed in a standard slump cone sags when the cone is removed.
# {{lb|en|Scotland|UK|dialect}} A [[boggy]] place.
# {{lb|en|Scotland}} The noise made by anything falling into a hole, or into a soft, [[miry]] place.
# {{lb|en|Scotland}} The [[gross]] [[amount]]; the [[mass]]; the [[lump]].
# {{lb|en|slang|by|_|extension}} A period when the person lives without [[sex]] when sex is expected or desired.
#* '''2004''', Jonathan Tolins, [https://books.google.com/books?id=G6MGnDzibpwC&pg=PA60&dq=slump+sex&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0CBsQ6AEwADhkahUKEwjJz5e0t9fIAhVJ5GMKHQxaC4s#v=onepage&q=slump%20sex&f=false The Last Sunday in June]
#*: "TOM. We haven't had sex with each other in five months.
#*: "MICHAEL. We're in a '''slump''', I know that."

